From b88979f28aacde95d62a58cefaeb039227f287d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:38:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] S3-1: docs measured on the rebased tree (numbers,
 ledger row 45, the not-met goal named)

GBA before / after on origin f91bd3e4 (libmgba): the four tours 574 -> 476 frames over 33 ms, the sim group 92 -> 22
(hub 0, shop 3, picker 6, pet 13 against a floor ROM with the resident updates off: 0 / 0 / 1 / 5). The sim now costs
0.3-1.2 ms of work in every tick (+0.4 ms mean over 50 windows), not the "~0.4 ms" the first notes said: corrected in
GBA.md, ROADMAP and SPEED_AUDIT3, with the windows that lost frames (Black Market 2 -> 7, news third tab 1 -> 2,
invaded 2 -> 3). The goal "no frame over 33 ms from the sim" is not met on the near-budget screens: said so, with
the two ways not taken (a cheaper update_resident_ex; skipping the pass on a long tick would tie the sim to frame
timing). PS1: code -12 B, the EXE ends where it did; sim group hub 29.96 -> 30.00. Dreamcast: no long tick before or
after (the stripped ELF and the nm file rebuilt first: the Flycast run needs them). Ledger row 41 -> 45.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
