 - **LV2, level script VM (2026-11-13, LEVELS round 2; docs/LEVELS.md "The level script VM"):** `core/src/lv_script.c` + `core/include/doomo/lv_script.h`: a deterministic bytecode interpreter (8 events, 20 actions, 32 byte variables, 16 actions a tick, 64 handlers / 2 KB, a queue of 16) with one host function for everything outside the VM; `tools/mapc.py` compiles `on EVENT [repeat] do ACTION ; ...` into `DoomoMapExt.script` and refuses what the VM would. Host tests per action and event, budgets, the checker, and a mapc-compiled script run twice with equal hashes. Nothing in the game calls it yet, so no byte on any platform (GBA sizes identical, PS1 EXE identical).
 - **Speed S3-3 (2026-11-13, the creator, speed audit 3; measured on libmgba and PCSX-Redux; docs/CREATOR.md "S3-3", docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 3: S3-3", docs/PS1.md "S3-3"):** the held creator frame (the saved G2-CR work) and creator panels drawn on the fast path before their capture (S2-6's recipe, `plat_ui_loops` before the pane). GBA: grid scrolled 17.2 -> 26.8 fps, rows 29.4 -> 30.0, a value held 22.2 -> 29.4, the picker 22.7 -> 29.1, hat grid 27.2 -> 29.8, try-on 15.2 -> 26.9, filter chip 21.7 -> 30.5; four tab changes still have two 50 ms frames, the held grid and the try-on stay under 30 (each step is a whole new bust: S3-2). PS1: the grid keeps its unpacked icons in the overlay scratch, grid scrolled 29.39 -> 30.00, try-on 28.57 -> 29.03; no resident byte (64 KB below the stack top with the FMV). Settled screens byte-identical; the pane's in-between frames come a tick later.
 - **No 3D character models inside houses (PS1-FLAT, 2026-11-13; the owner: "disabled the 3d models of your player character and vice versa when you are inside their houses - save up some ram there", `OWNER_DECISIONS.md` "HOUSE CHARACTERS FLAT"; measured on PCSX-Redux; docs/PS1.md "No 3D models in houses", section 7):** only the PS1 drew a 3D figure in the house, the player's chibi (`model.c`). `ps1/src/room.c` now draws the player with the same `billboard()` as every resident, visitor, guest and demon, from the body sprite the core hands over (direction, walk frame, sit squash; the picture the GBA and the Dreamcast show, and the avatar being played), in Build, Live, Photo, Score, Hold the Door and a visit; it keeps its contact shadow and still rests in the kept backdrop while it stands still. With the house out, `model.c` (4,132 B) left resident RAM for the combat overlay group: `ovl_plan.py` `PLAT_GROUPS` / `GUARDED`, and `plat_view3d()` asks `ovl_code_in()` before it draws the model (the plan fails if house code, or anything else, would call it; `ps1/tools/test_ovl_guard.py`, 6 tests, in CI). The house's hooks in the 3D code are gone (`g_model_hold`, `g_r3_area`). **PS1 game disc with the boot FMV: 65,952 -> 70,480 B below the stack top (+4,528 B); on the tip it landed on (`19d01fe`) 68,224 -> 72,736 B (+4,512 B), 992 B under the 72 KB gate**; the slot keeps its 131,072 B (combat group 124,056 -> 128,188 B, home 130,856 -> 129,420 B). `prims.c` (3,612 B) stays resident: with it the combat group would pass the slot. House fps (`home.txt`, on the landing tip): plain 30.17 -> 30.17, steady 29.39 -> 30.00, orbit 27.17 -> 30.00, cellar (stress layout) 27.80 -> 27.80, defend stress (stress layout) 19.10 -> 22.78, modal 29.19 -> 30.00, Hold the Door wave 3 30.13 -> 30.13 (15.1 -> 6.5 ms of CPU), visit 30.17 -> 30.17; the speed tour's 19 house windows all hold 30 (the busy Live layout 28.78 -> 30.00). Third-person combat is unchanged: `perf_combat`'s shots are byte-identical, fps 29.5-30.0 as before. The core, the GBA and the Dreamcast are untouched (no file of theirs changed).
-- **Speed S3-1 (2026-11-13, the sim's 15-minute pass, speed audit 3 miss 5; measured on libmgba, PCSX-Redux and Flycast; docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 3: S3-1"):** the resident pass moves with the clock: the cursor earns slots at a steady 1,000 per 15 game minutes whatever the day length and speed (`SIM_PASS_NUM` / `SIM_PASS_DEN`, a `uint16_t` credit in the padding of `SimState`; `SIM_BATCH` 32 -> 16 is the hard cap), so a resident is updated once per interval and a tick does one update at the default clock (15 at the fastest) instead of 32 residents in 32 ticks every 15 minutes; a visit that would live under 8 game minutes (the first passes after `sim_init`, a load, a fast-forward) leaves the stamp alone, so no minute is lost or counted twice; the stamps and the cursor are not saved, a load runs `sim_init`: no migration. A new bond in the sorted edge table is made room for with a halfword move on the GBA (libc `memmove` copied the 4.6 KB byte by byte: 3-7 ms in one tick). GBA drawn fps: shop gifts tab 21.5 -> **30.0**, apartments 25.7 -> **30.0**, Options Accessibility 23.7 / 28.2 -> **30.0**, pet-care boss 28.6 -> **30.0**, citizen picker 22.9 -> 29.7, pet 28.5 -> 29.8; frames over 33 ms in the four tours 575 -> 489. Not the same sim on purpose (another update order, the same rates): `test_sim_x4` and the news-stream golden of `test_sim` are recorded again. EWRAM / IWRAM unchanged (ledger row 48). New speed2 group `sim` (four 1,200-tick windows with the pass inside; GBA gates `expect-fps 29.8`, `expect-gap 51`). **Still short:** windows within ~3 ms of the budget (pet, picker, Black Market, news tab) lose a frame now and then to the sim's steady ~0.4 ms a tick: S3-13.
+- **Speed S3-1 (2026-11-13, the sim's 15-minute pass, speed audit 3 miss 5; measured on libmgba, PCSX-Redux and Flycast; docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 3: S3-1"):** the resident pass moves with the clock: the cursor earns slots at a steady 1,000 per 15 game minutes whatever the day length and speed (`SIM_PASS_NUM` / `SIM_PASS_DEN`, a `uint16_t` credit in the padding of `SimState`; `SIM_BATCH` 32 -> 16 is the hard cap), so a resident is updated once per interval and a tick does one update at the default clock (15 at the fastest) instead of 32 residents in 32 ticks every 15 minutes; a visit that would live under 8 game minutes (the first passes after `sim_init`, a load, a fast-forward) leaves the stamp alone, so no minute is lost or counted twice; the stamps and the cursor are not saved, a load runs `sim_init`: no migration. A new bond in the sorted edge table is made room for with a halfword move on the GBA (libc `memmove` copied the 4.6 KB byte by byte: 3-7 ms in one tick). GBA drawn fps (origin `f91bd3e4` before and after): shop gifts tab 21.5 -> **30.0**, apartments 25.2 -> **30.0**, Options Accessibility 23.7 / 28.2 -> **30.0**, pet-care boss 28.6 -> **30.0**, citizen picker 22.9 -> 29.5, pet 28.5 -> 29.8; frames over 33 ms in the four tours 574 -> 476. PS1: the island hub window 4 frames of 50 ms -> 0; Dreamcast: no long tick before or after. Not the same sim on purpose (another update order, the same rates): `test_sim_x4` and the news-stream golden of `test_sim` are recorded again. EWRAM / IWRAM unchanged (ledger row 48); PS1 resident -12 B, the EXE ends where it did (0x801ef580). New speed2 group `sim` (four 1,200-tick windows with the pass inside; GBA gates `expect-gap 51` and fps floors 29.8 / 29.5). **Not met:** "no frame over 33 ms from the sim" on the near-budget GBA screens: the work now arrives as 0.3-1.2 ms in every tick (+0.4 ms mean over 50 windows against a floor ROM with the resident updates off), so the sim group still has 0 / 3 / 6 / 13 single 50 ms frames (hub / shop / picker / pet; floor 0 / 0 / 1 / 5) and Black Market 2 -> 7: S3-13 (menu headroom), or a cheaper `update_resident_ex`.
 - **Real stick support (ST1, 2026-11-08; the owner: "actual dualshock/stick support so I don't have to move the camera controls with wacky controlling"; measured on PCSX-Redux and Flycast; docs/PS1.md "Sticks", docs/DREAMCAST.md 5):** PS1: a DualShock no longer needs its ANALOG button: when a pad shows up (boot or hot-plug) and reads digital, `ps1/src/pad.c` sends the config sequence (43h / 44h 01 03 analog + lock / 43h) over SIO0 between two BIOS polls (three tries, a digital pad is left alone); L3 / R3 read (`BTN_L3` / `BTN_R3`). Options > Controls gains **Auto** (the new default; Classic / Auto / Dual stick / Modern): Dual stick while an analog pad is plugged in, Modern otherwise, live; explicit Classic / Modern win; saves' old default Modern (stored 1) reads as Auto, an explicit Modern is stored as 3 (`controls_scheme()`). The sticks drive: the shooter (left walk / strafe, right turn / look, R3 lock-on), the overworld (analog walk in any direction: creep, walk, run at the rim), the house view (a right-stick flick = one 90-degree step, repeat on hold; build, live, photo), the creator (the right stick spins the citizen: the turntable opens as a peek). Dreamcast (Auto): the stick's X turns, Y walks, the analog triggers strafe by pressure, both triggers lock on; the overworld walks off the stick. Shared dead zone / curve in `input.c` (`stick_dz`, `stick_curve`, `input_rflick`). Prompts, the control card and the shooter tip follow the scheme in effect; Dual stick on a digital pad says "Analog sticks: use a DualShock". Tests: `core/tests/test_sticks.c` (scheme resolution, dead zone / curve, flick repeat, trigger strafe, each consumer), `dc/tests/vmu` (caps / triggers), harness `stick LX LY RX RY` on the PS1 (`ps1/harness/scripts/sticks.txt`; `sticks_auto.txt` with `run.py --analog-pad`: Redux's DualShock powering up digital is switched by the game, "pad: analog", the card still saves, the D-pad still drives), the native runner and dcrun (`dc/tests/sticks/sticks.txt`)