 - **Speed S2-4, first family (2026-11-08, the Fun Fair's kept playfield, speed audit 2 cause C3; measured on libmgba and PCSX-Redux; docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 2: S2-4", docs/PS1.md "Speed tour 2"):** a fair game may split its playfield into still parts, baked into the GBA ROM per key with its own drawing code (`DOOMO_BACKDROP_MG`, SP7's baker), and live parts drawn over a whole-picture copy each frame; still parts the usual order draws over live ones (a hole's front over the rising critter, the sign board over the peeking imps) are put back from the ROM in their own spans. Exact (`test_stage`: Whack's bot rounds with the kept picture on / off, every frame identical; every key baked). Whack-an-Imp: GBA 15.1 -> 20.9 fps Sweet, 15.0 -> 20.0 Hellfire (57.5 -> 40.3 / 61.5 -> 44.9 ms); ROM +1.15 MB, EWRAM -8 B (ledger row 40), PS1 compiled out (65 KB below the stack top with the FMV, unchanged by S2-4). **Still short of 30 / not done:** Whack's live part (imps, critters, HUD text; next: OBJ sprites, partial copies), the other fair games (Gallery 11, Derby 22, Dodge 21-27, Memory Hellfire 21.5 fps), the kitchen (17-22), dreams (11-13), cutscenes (10-23), library lobby / jukebox (20) and studio STAGE (23): S2-4 stays open for them.
 - **Speed S2-5 (2026-11-08, scaled art, speed audit 2 cause C4; measured on libmgba and PCSX-Redux; docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 2: S2-5", docs/PS1.md "Speed tour 2"):** instead of pre-scaled ROM copies (the weapon plans and the welding icon are composed at run time, and the scale-1 blit reading ROM is no faster), the GBA draws every scale-2..4 image through `vid_blitn`, an ARM loop of the IWRAM UI group (a source row expanded once, then word copies of its opaque runs on each covered row; exact, `blit2test`), asked for by the cutscenes, the weapons wing and the welding game (`plat_ui_loops`); the Derby's racers become 8bpp pictures in the scene scratch drawn with the scale-1 blit instead of a `plat_rect` per colour run; the welding seam and bead are drawn as runs of same-y columns. All exact (`vhash-seq` against `c0dc4ba`). GBA drawn fps: weapons frames 24.9 -> **30**, weld intro 22.2 -> **30**, welding 21.5 -> **29.9** (every frame 2 vblanks), Derby races 15.0 -> 22.1-22.6, Vapula vignette 12.0 -> 16.1; PS1 unchanged at 30 (welding 30.12); no Dreamcast run (these scenes already held 30 there). GBA EWRAM / IWRAM unchanged (ledger row 39), PS1 resident unchanged (65 KB below the stack top with the FMV). `expect-fps` floors 28 / 20 / 14. Still short: the Derby (38 ms: sky, grandstand and bunting) and the Vapula and home vignettes (sky bands, puffs, the full-screen wallpaper): S2-4's held backdrops.
